      "writtenOn": "2023-03-21T23:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it may be safer to set `flash_set_protect_rc \u003d EC_RES_BUSY;` rather than in the deferred function. The deferred function won\u0027t get called until 100 ms later, so if another `FLASH_PROTECT_ASYNC` comes in during the meantime we\u0027ll call this again, which is not what we want. (I think that\u0027s a bug in the [example you\u0027re using](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/flash.c;l\u003d1440?q\u003dEC_CMD_FLASH_ERASE\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch\u0026start\u003d31). Can you create a CL to fix it there too?)",
      "range": {
